Group] and the establishment of a UK subsidiary, [l=Strictly Rhythm UK]. This partnership ultimately led to the label's demise nine months later, in October 2002.\r\nAfter four years of legal wrangling, Mark Finkelstein regained control of the label, its trademark and its recordings and publishing rights and relaunched the label in 2007 in partnership with [l=Defected], with Phil Cheeseman as A&R manager.\r\nA&R from 2011 to 2013: [a=Dave Lambert].\r\nIn 2013 the label's catalogue was acquired by BMG Rights Management, with the label continuing to release new recordings.\r\nIn 2019 the brand name was acquired by BMG.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:609","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":287001,"name":"Strictly Rhythm Records, Inc."},"sublabels":[{"id":7599,"name":"Grandslam Records"},{"id":96215,"name":"Ill Friction"},{"id":7771,"name":"Phat Wax Records"},{"id":95802,"name":"Physical Graffiti Music"},{"id":15199,"name":"Pink Music"},{"id":129335,"name":"Red Stick Recordings"},{"id":417450,"name":"Strictly Rhythm UK"},{"id":243667,"name":"Xtra Life Records"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/609-Strictly-Rhythm","type":"label","urls":["http://strictlyrhythm.bio.to/links","http://www.facebook.com/strictlyrhythm","http://instagram.com/strictlyrhythm","http://linktr.ee/StrictlyRhythm","http://www.mixcloud.com/StrictlyRhythm","http://soundcloud.com/strictlyrhythm","http://vimeo.com/strictlyrhythm","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strictly_Rhythm","http://x.com/strictlyrhythm","http://www.youtube.com/StrictlyRhythmVideo"]}},"/api/discogs/label/62136/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"62136","image":"https://i.discogs.com/udXpMPeMKu_TSb4VTKwXY3ICFOvikTMwNAymitHJSEM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:268/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTYyMTM2/LTE2NjM4Nzg5MTAt/OTk4Ni5wbmc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/4lwXzMEzQYk5i0VZvPbJdoTQnULABkq6Ph4GQxyTnEY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTYyM